{"type":"message","id":"426759e9","parentId":"7c0ae1f8","timestamp":"2026-03-28T01:15:44.297Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No logs found. Let me try to find out what happened with the cron job. Let me check if there's a workspace file that was supposed to be generated by the briefing cron.\n\nActually, let me focus on what I need to do:\n1. The user didn't receive a morning briefing\n2. There's a cron job that should run at 8:00 AM\n3. It ran (1h ago) but apparently didn't produce a briefing\n\nLet me check what the briefing cron is actually supposed to do - maybe it's set up to run a specific script or agent task. Let me look at the cron configuration.","thinkingSignature":"6b3094a327a891e28bdbf69d29a894f3b8644d342d26ba2e34cfd977c9e6e6a3"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_lahvj81cbddj_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron get morning-briefing 2>/dev/null || cat /root/.openclaw/openclaw.json | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); crons=d.get('cron',{}).get('jobs',[]); [print(json.dumps(c, indent=2)) for c in crons if 'briefing' in c.get('name','').lower()]\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":4005,"output":236,"cacheRead":22858,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27099,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774660539213}}
