{"type":"message","id":"fb818089","parentId":"867162fc","timestamp":"2026-03-28T05:12:54.100Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All bindings are empty arrays! That means none of the agents are explicitly bound to any chats. But earlier we saw that group messages ARE routing to the main agent. \n\nLooking at the inbound metadata in this very conversation: `\"chat_id\": \"user:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\"` and `\"chat_type\": \"direct\"` - this is a direct message.\n\nBut the user said \"群聊里没回复\" (not replying in group chat). The group is `oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3`.\n\nWait - the issue might be that when the cron agents try to send to the group, they can't because there's no channel binding configured for that group. \n\nSo they're probably defaulting to direct messages instead. The cron jobs show \"delivered: true\" in the logs, but that doesn't necessarily mean it reached the right place - the agent might just be defaulting to my direct chat with the user rather than posting in the actual group where it should be going.\n\nI need to look at the cron configuration for the community scan job to understand where it's actually configured to deliver results.","thinkingSignature":"926d244df211ff1448e0a7c1d1049af19585081d5d0025b40c34fd7d05276c84"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_eewwdjtlsqv5_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\njobs = d.get('jobs',[])\nfor j in jobs:\n    if 'community' in j.get('name','').lower() or 'scan' in j.get('name','').lower() or j.get('id','') == '6f8bd6c8-5b5f-4cf7-8e6f-3479fd23fc64':\n        print(json.dumps(j, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n        print('---')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":20421,"output":397,"cacheRead":22858,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43676,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0