{"type":"message","id":"0b26bfad","parentId":"0e9da60d","timestamp":"2026-03-28T05:13:08.238Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! The `delivery.mode` is `\"none\"` and `lastDelivered: false`. This means xixi's cron job is NOT configured to send results to any chat. The instructions say \"禁止向任何聊天渠道发消息\" (no sending to any chat channels).\n\nBut earlier we saw that xixi was sending messages via `sessions_send` to the main agent. Looking at the message from xixi at 11:48 - that was a `sessions_send` to the main agent, not a channel message.\n\nThe issue is that xixi sent results to `main` via `sessions_send`, but main never forwarded those to the group chat `oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3`.\n\n\nI need to figure out what the user means by \"群聊\" - it could be the OpenClaw project group or the default chat. Looking back at the MEMORY.md, there's a group `oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3` where only OpenClaw project updates should be reported. The cron run shows \"delivered\": true but that's separate from the `sessions_send` to main. The real problem is that xixi's scan results are reaching main via `sessions_send`, but main isn't forwarding them to the designated group chat like it should.\n\nThe user mentioned I stopped replying in the group chat - but when I look at the conversation, I'm receiving direct messages from the user (ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8) and replying to them, which appears to be working fine. So either the group chat delivery is actually failing silently, or the user is referring to something else entirely that I'm not seeing in the conversation log. The issue is likely that the cron agent uses `sessions_send` to report to main, but main then needs to forward that to the group chat—and either that forwarding step isn't happening, or it's failing. I should check what channels are actually configured in the bindings to understand where messages are supposed to go.","thinkingSignature":"b38cd