{"type":"message","id":"2f98b80a","parentId":"bac296ac","timestamp":"2026-03-28T11:06:44.756Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, sent to the group. Now let me respond to the inter-session message from xixi.","thinkingSignature":"6bec6b241e930e4f9ae23db4b34dc10feb0a24987bb6095be61d0a9b66996177"},{"type":"text","text":"xixi 扫描结果已入库 + 同步群里。\n\n**关于 #56240**：这个 PR 修的正好可能是 #56347 的根因——plugin registry 在 pinned 和 active 之间不一致。如果 #56240 先 merge，#56347 就不用单独提了；如果 #56240 卡住，#56347 就补一个针对性 fix。\n\n**关于 #56326**：PR #56342 已经在修，盯着 #56342 等 merge 就好，不需要另外 action。\n\n**待确认**：群里已同步进展，xixi 每小时 `sessions_send → main` 的问题——如果群里希望实时看到每小时 alert，告诉我，我把 xixi cron 的 delivery 改成直接 announce 到群；如果每天 9 点那条够用，就保持现状。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":27448,"output":180,"cacheRead":22392,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":50020,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774695997944,"responseId":"0616e93e97d341f988216cb062c31f4e"}}
{"type":"message","id":"64dfa57e","parentId":"2f98b80a","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:48:01.813Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b5348913160a8b494bfe6933481e\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"sender\": \"范\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sat 2026-03-28 20:47 GMT+8\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"范 (ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n  \"name\": \"范\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b5348913160a8b494bfe6933481e]\n范: 你在群里又没回复我了"}],"timestamp":1774702081791}}
{"type":"message","id":"042a9256","parentId":"64dfa57e","timestamp":"2026-03-28T12:48:31.384Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying I didn't reply in the group chat again. Let me check what's happening. \n\nWait - I did just send a message to the group chat (`oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3`) in my previous response. But the user is saying there's no reply. \n\nLet me think... The user might be referring to a different issue - maybe the group chat messages that xixi sends via `sessions_send` are not reaching the group, and they're asking me to fix this.\n\nActually, I think I already fixed this by:\n1. Manually sending the update to the group\n\n\n2. Creating a daily 9 AM cron that announces to the group\n\nBut xixi's direct `sessions_send` messages to me are still only coming to my main session - they never make it to the group. The user is probably referring to xixi's reports, not my replies. The issue is that xixi uses `sessions_send` which delivers to my main session, but I don't have an automatic relay set up to forward those messages to the group. The daily 9 AM summary is configured to announce to the group, so I need to check if that's working properly or if there's something else preventing group replies.\n\nLooking at what the user said - \"你在群里又没回复我了\" - they're saying I didn't reply in the group chat AGAIN. This suggests that either my previous message to the group didn't actually go through or wasn't visible, or they're saying that when they message in the group, I'm not responding there. The issue is likely that when someone messages the group, my replies are going to the wrong place instead of staying in the group.\n\nThe problem is probably related to how the binding works - if the Feishu group isn't explicitly bound in the configuration, incoming messages might be falling back to the default agent but my replies could still be routing to the main session instead of back to the group. Let me check the group binding configuration to see what's actually set up there.\n\nI notice the bindings are all empty across the accounts, but xixi's `sessions_send` only delivers to the main session, not to the group. So if the user is in the group and I send a reply from my main session, it might not be reaching the group at all - I need to figure out whether my replies are actually going to the group channel or just staying in the main session. The issue is likely that when someone messages the group, OpenClaw routes it to the main agent session instead of keeping the conversation in the group itself. I need to either configure explicit group bindings or set up a relay mechanism so group messages get properly forwarded and responded to in the group chat. I need to check what chat the user is currently in by looking at the inbound metadata - the `chat_id` shows this is a direct message to me, not the group chat. So the user is reporting that when they message me directly, I reply correctly, but when they're in the group chat `oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3`, I'm not responding there. This suggests the group might not be properly configured to receive replies, or my responses aren't being routed back to the group correctly. 我意识到用户可能在两个不同的地方和我互动——飞书私聊和群聊——但我的回复可能没有正确路由到群聊频道。问题可能出在 groupPolicy 或 requireMention 的配置上，导致我的响应被发送到了错误的会话。我需要检查 OpenClaw 的配置，看看群聊的路由是否正确设置，以及为什么我的回复没有到达群聊而是发送到了私聊。 I need to check the gateway status and recent logs to see what's actually happening with the group routing, then verify the group binding configuration to understand why replies might not be going through.","thinkingSignature":"d442af8f0899b94984f3f4900ba884869a61dc56e65f09b46afbcfe712efec84"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0l9g5o27zc6b_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw gateway status 2>/dev/null | head -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":80,"output":820,"cacheRead":9469,"cacheWrite":40515,"totalTokens":50884,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774702081813,"responseId":"0617010255a889601d99f8de78d738ac"}}
